# Pairs with NoKeyLost. The undo moves the alias back with a map that is not
# the one captured when the resize began, so a key routes to a shard of the
# old copy that never held it.
MODULE: NoKeyLostUndoRestoresForeignMap
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the undo moves the alias back with a map that routes a key to a shard the old copy never held it on
PERTURBS: UndoSwap

--- FIND
    /\ alias' = T
    /\ rmap' = rmapOld
    /\ published' = published \cup {<<T, rmapOld>>}
--- REPLACE
    /\ alias' = T
\* MUTATION: the restored map is not the captured one.
    /\ rmap' = s2
    /\ published' = published \cup {<<T, s2>>}
--- END
